<title>MOROCCO: France grants Morocco $27.5 mln credit for dams.</title>
<headline>France grants Morocco $27.5 mln credit for dams.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French Development Bank (Caisse Francaise de Developpement - CFD) and Morocco on Monday signed a loan agreement for 171 million francs ($27.5 million) which Morocco will use to build three dams.</p>
<p>Moroccan Finance Minister Mohamed Kabbaj signed the accord with CFD director Olivier Beugnot, the ministry said.</p>
<p>The loan will be repaid over 20 years, with seven years grace, at an annual interest rate of three percent.</p>
</text>
